### z47 Zig port ###
# Zig build cache and output
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# z47-owned roots that a re-imported upstream .gitignore would swallow. Upstream
# ignores a root `/build` (its meson/make output dir) and z47 owns a `build/`
# directory of Zig build logic; without these negations an import of that rule
# would silently stop new owner files from being added.
#
# gitignore resolves by LAST MATCH, so this only works while the imported block
# stays ABOVE this section -- which is how the file is laid out and how a
# hand-reconciled import must keep it. That ordering is not left to trust:
# check-source-ownership.sh asserts every z47-owned root is unignored, so an
# import that outranks these negations fails the gate instead of going unnoticed.
# Delete them only together with the directories they protect.
!/build/
!/src/
!/docs/
!/bridge/

# Python bytecode cache (governance scripts under .github/project/)
__pycache__/

# Coverage instrumentation output (zig build coverage -> report-zig-coverage.sh)
cov_pcs.txt

# Maintainer working surface: planning/audit docs and reports. Policy is to
# never commit this tree; ignore it so it cannot be staged
# by accident.
__DEV/

# Python tooling (pyproject.toml / .pre-commit-config.yaml). Everything here is
# a local cache or a local environment: reproducibility comes from the pinned
# `rev:`s in .pre-commit-config.yaml and the version floors in pyproject.toml,
# so there is nothing to commit. uv.lock is ignored rather than tracked, which
# is what the sibling ports do -- there is no Python package to install and no
# deployment to reproduce, only three dev tools.
.venv/
uv.lock
.ruff_cache/
.ty_cache/
